            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0310" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11290: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-10T12:00:00+08:00">November 10,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 10—6:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>112. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 10, noon. Steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Ifung</hi> and
                            lighter No. 1, both of Yangtze Rapid Company, fired upon at three
                            different places by trench mortars and rifles on Saturday<anchor n="14"
                                xml:id="d254-f1"/> between Chenglingki and Ichang. American naval
                            guard on <hi rendition="#italic">Ifung</hi> returned fire in each case
                                <pb facs="0311" n="213" xml:id="pg213"/> of attack on that vessel.
                            Resumption of through passenger traffic between Hankow and Peiping
                            announced by Railway Administration effective today. This marks first
                            through train service between Hankow and Peiping since approximately
                            March 15, 1930. Repeated to the Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
